Subject: [PATCH] C14, patch 6 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M25, answer 2):
 THE PLAN OF 2026-10-29 LEAVES THE PUBLIC FACE'S LIST; IT IS LABELLED AT ITS
 HEAD AS A DATED PROPOSAL OF THE WORKING RECORD, AND THE README CALLS IT SO

Main's M25, answer 2: the plan of 2026-10-29 is off the public face's list; it is labelled at its head as a dated
proposal, part of the working record; the README's line, which already calls it the order of work chosen on
2026-10-30, adds "a dated document of the working record".

- docs/THE_FINAL_ATTACK_2026-10-29.md: one line under its title, in italics: "A dated proposal of 2026-10-29, part of
  the working record. The order of work it proposes was chosen on 2026-10-30; its words are kept as written. (Label
  added 2026-11-13.)" No word of the plan changes.
- scripts/gates/gates.py: the plan leaves PUBLIC_FACE; its held counts leave PUBLIC_FACE_HELD, with a comment that
  says when and why. The gate reads 13 pages (4 at zero, 1,376 words held).
- README.md: the line on the plan ends "the order of work chosen on 2026-10-30, a dated document of the working
  record".
- tests/test_public_face.py: one test holds the three (the plan off the list and the held counts, the label as the
  page's first line after its title, the README's words), and a plant (the label taken out) that it refuses.

The public face's tests, B1028's ledger test (which lists the plan among dated documents) and the README's test:
22 passed.

0 of 19.
